MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every route previously shipped an identical ~90-word client-side shell carrying
the homepage <title> and a canonical pointing at '/'. GPTBot, OAI-SearchBot,
ChatGPT-User, ClaudeBot, PerplexityBot, Amazonbot, meta-externalagent and CCBot
do not execute JavaScript (Bingbot ~1%), so the site was invisible to every AI
answer engine, and Googlebot's raw-HTML pass read a homepage canonical on all
~30 URLs.

- scripts/prerender.mjs: postbuild puppeteer pass renders all 28 routes and
  writes real per-route HTML (own title/meta/canonical/JSON-LD/body). Reduced
  concurrency + serial retry for the heavy three.js pages. Body <noscript>
  fallback stripped from prerendered output (kept in template).
- Host standardized on apex https://floguardfl.com across Seo.jsx, index.html,
  robots.txt, llms.txt, sitemap generator, _redirects (www→apex, matching the
  live zone-level redirect that already sends www→apex).
- Schema: LocalBusiness → HomeAndConstructionBusiness; REMOVED self-serving
  aggregateRating (ineligible + manual-action risk per Google review-snippet
  policy); added email, openingHoursSpecification, hasOfferCatalog (4 Service
  offers), Facebook sameAs.
- Sitemap: real lastmod from git history per data file (was: today's date on
  every URL, every build).
- robots.txt: strategy comments removed (robots.txt is public).
- _redirects: 301 /pricing → cost-guide post, /franchise → /contact (both
  indexed but route-less, serving the empty shell as soft-404s).
- Meta description 168 → 150 chars.
- Root package.json: stripped UTF-8 BOM (broke cosmiconfig/any JSON parser
  walking up from frontend/).

Verified: 28/28 prerendered files pass — unique titles, self-canonicals on
apex, ≥250 words delivered text, JSON-LD present, no aggregateRating, no www
leaks.

