Three new blog posts targeting SERPs with zero real local competition, plus the
sump-pumps service page expanded 445 → ~1,100 words:

- /blog/volusia-county-drainage-permits — quotes Volusia LDC §72-777(b)(1)(a)
  single-family exemption, §72-777(b)(1)(f) 1,000 sq ft threshold, §72-777(b)(3)
  erosion rule, and the city-vs-county jurisdiction split (county governs
  stormwater only in unincorporated areas). City-by-city table incl. Port Orange
  Ch. 58 ROW permit + Engineering (386) 506-5538.
- /blog/french-drain-cost-daytona-beach — honest $4,500–$12,000 band per the
  pricing playbook (never per-foot), coastal drivers: 40–60 in wet-season water
  table, salt-air specs, beachside access, battery backup.
- /blog/french-drain-not-working-florida — fine-sand infiltration failure mode
  no northern guide covers, symptoms timeline, depth-trap diagnosis, honest
  repair-vs-rebuild call.
- sump-pumps service: decision logic for when a sump is required vs a waste of
  money, install spec, hurricane/battery guidance, discharge legality, 6 FAQs.

New category "Local Rules". Every post opens with a direct, quotable answer in
the first ~200 chars after the H1 (ChatGPT instant-mode indexing window).
Sitemap regenerated: 31 URLs, apex host. Prerender verified: 31/31 routes,
unique titles/canonicals, zero www refs.

